  1: # AI Prompting Guide for Scholar-Flow
  2: 
  3: > **TL;DR**: Write `AGENTS.md` **once** per project and update it when conventions change. Don't rewrite it every session. Use model-specific strategies below to maximize cache hits and output quality.
  4: 
  5: ---
  6: 
  7: ## Table of Contents
  8: 
  9: 1. [AGENTS.md: Write Once, Update as Needed](#agentsmd-write-once-update-as-needed)
 10: 2. [Model-Specific Prompting Strategies](#model-specific-prompting-strategies)
 11: 3. [Scenario-Based Prompting Examples](#scenario-based-prompting-examples)
 12: 4. [Prefix Caching Best Practices](#prefix-caching-best-practices)
 13: 5. [Prompt Structure Templates](#prompt-structure-templates)
 14: 6. [Anti-Patterns to Avoid](#anti-patterns-to-avoid)
 15: 
 16: ---
 17: 
 18: ## AGENTS.md: Write Once, Update as Needed
 19: 
 20: ### What is AGENTS.md?
 21: 
 22: `AGENTS.md` is a **persistent project context file** that lives in your project root. It tells AI agents:
 23: - Project architecture and tech stack
 24: - Coding conventions and rules
 25: - File structure and where things live
 26: - Critical security rules (Stripe, S3, auth)
 27: - Commands and workflows
 28: 
 29: ### Do NOT Rewrite AGENTS.md Every Session
 30: 
 31: **Wrong approach:**
 32: ```
 33: User: "Write AGENTS.md with these rules..."
 34: AI: [writes full AGENTS.md]
 35: Next session:
 36: User: "Write AGENTS.md again with updated rules..."
 37: AI: [rewrites entire file]
 38: ```
 39: 
 40: **Correct approach:**
 41: ```
 42: User: "Update AGENTS.md to add the new Stripe webhook rule"
 43: AI: [edits only the relevant section, preserving the rest]
 44: ```
 45: 
 46: ### When to Update AGENTS.md
 47: 
 48: | Trigger | Action |
 49: |---------|--------|
 50: | New coding convention added | Append to relevant section |
 51: | Architecture change | Update structure section |
 52: | New critical rule (security, auth) | Add to "Never Do" / "Always Do" |
 53: | New command added | Add to "Exact Commands" |
 54: | Phase completed | Update "Current Status" |
 55: | Cache model changes | Update "Multi-Model Cache Optimization" |
 56: 
 57: ### When to Regenerate Repomix
 58: 
 59: Run `yarn repomix` when:
 60: - Major structural changes (new directories, moved files)
 61: - New dependencies or build tools added
 62: - Before asking a new AI agent to work on the project
 63: - When context seems stale (agent doesn't know about recent changes)
 64: 
 65: ---
 66: 
 67: ## Model-Specific Prompting Strategies
 68: 
 69: ### DeepSeek V4 Pro / Flash
 70: 
 71: **Characteristics:**
 72: - Cache hits from **byte 0** on matching prefix
 73: - Excellent for long-context reasoning
 74: - Strong code generation
 75: - Cost-effective for repeated queries
 76: 
 77: **Prompting Strategy:**
 78: ```markdown
 79: # CACHE OPTIMIZATION CONTRACT
 80: # This exact block must be first. Never modify.
 81: 
 82: [Your project context here - static between calls]
 83: 
 84: ---
 85: 
 86: ## Current Task
 87: [Task-specific context - changes per session]
 88: 
 89: ## Goal
 90: [One sentence goal]
 91: 
 92: ## Files to Read
 93: 1. [file path]
 94: 2. [file path]
 95: 
 96: ## Implementation Approach
 97: [Your approach]
 98: ```
 99: 
100: **Example:**
101: ```
102: Goal: Fix the auth middleware token expiration bug
103: Files to Read: 
104: 1. apps/backend/src/app/middleware/auth.ts
105: 2. apps/backend/src/app/errors/ApiError.ts
106: 
107: Approach: Check the JWT verify logic, look for clock skew issues,
108: add a 5-minute leeway for token expiration.
109: ```
110: 
111: ---
112: 
113: ### Kimi K2.6
114: 
115: **Characteristics:**
116: - Cache hits from **byte 0** on matching prefix
117: - Excellent reasoning and context understanding
118: - Strong at following complex multi-step instructions
119: - Good at maintaining context across long conversations
120: 
121: **Prompting Strategy:**
122: - Be explicit about step ordering
123: - Use numbered lists for multi-step tasks
124: - Provide clear success criteria
125: 
126: **Example:**
127: ```
128: Goal: Implement Phase 2.1 auth pages with figma-make design
129: 
130: Steps (execute in order):
131: 1. Read figma-make/pages/LoginPage.tsx and RegisterPage.tsx
132: 2. Create apps/frontend/src/app/login/page.tsx with figma-make design
133: 3. Create apps/frontend/src/app/register/page.tsx with figma-make design
134: 4. Run yarn type-check after each file
135: 5. Update IMPLEMENTATION.md to mark Phase 2.1 items as [x]
136: 
137: Success Criteria:
138: - All 5 auth pages render with figma-make design
139: - Type-check passes
140: - No console errors
141: ```
142: 
143: ---
144: 
145: ### GLM-4 / MiMo
146: 
147: **Characteristics:**
148: - Cache hits from **byte 0** on matching prefix
149: - Strong Chinese-English bilingual capability
150: - Good at structured output
151: 
152: **Prompting Strategy:**
153: - Use clear delimiters (---, ###)
154: - Structure output expectations explicitly
155: 
156: **Example:**
157: ```
158: ## Input
159: File: apps/frontend/src/components/sections/Hero.tsx
160: 
161: ## Required Changes
162: 1. Add "Simple 5-Step Workflow" badge above heading
163: 2. Update heading to "Your research workflow, reimagined"
164: 3. Add gradient text effect on "reimagined"
165: 
166: ## Expected Output
167: Return the COMPLETE updated file content.
168: Do not summarize or truncate.
169: ```
170: 
171: ---
172: 
173: ### Qwen 3.x
174: 
175: **Characteristics:**
176: - Requires **minimum 1024 tokens** to activate prefix caching
177: - Shorter prompts may not benefit from caching
178: - Excellent for reasoning and tool use
179: 
180: **Prompting Strategy:**
181: - Ensure AGENTS.md + skills content stays above 1024 tokens
182: - Don't shorten the frozen prefix block
183: - Add detailed context to activate cache
184: 
185: **Example:**
186: ```
187: # Project: Scholar-Flow (1.1.0)
188: # Architecture: Turborepo + Next.js 15 + Express + Prisma + PostgreSQL
189: # Current Phase: Phase 2 - Auth & Onboarding
190: # Status: 5 of 6 auth pages pending
191: 
192: [Detailed project context... ensure this exceeds 1024 tokens]
193: 
194: ---
195: 
196: ## Task
197: Implement the forgot-password page matching figma-make design.
198: 
199: ## Context
200: - figma-make source: figma-make/pages/ForgotPasswordPage.tsx
201: - Target location: apps/frontend/src/app/forgot-password/page.tsx
202: - Must use "use client" and Link from next/link
203: - Must not include Navbar/Footer (layout provides them)
204: 
205: ## Files to Read
206: 1. figma-make/pages/ForgotPasswordPage.tsx
207: 2. apps/frontend/src/components/ui/card-variants.tsx
208: 3. apps/frontend/src/components/ui/button.tsx
209: 
210: ## Output
211: Return the complete file content. Do not truncate.
212: ```
