133: ## Authentication Rules
134: Frontend: NextAuth.js only — Google/GitHub OAuth + email/password.
135: Backend: JWT + bcrypt + refresh tokens.
136: NEVER suggest better-auth or any auth replacement.
137: NEVER bypass auth middleware on protected routes.
138: NEVER store raw passwords — always bcrypt.
139: Session validation: backend verifies JWT, frontend uses NextAuth session.
140: 
141: ### Auth-state persistence (learned the hard way in 1.2.2)
142: 
143: After any auth-state dispatch (`setCredentials` / `clearCredentials`) and BEFORE any `window.location.href` navigation, you MUST `await persistor.flush()`. redux-persist schedules localStorage writes on a microtask; a hard navigation kills that microtask and the next page rehydrates stale state. The 401 cascade and "wrong user shown" bugs in 1.2.1 came from skipping this.
144: 
145: - `apps/frontend/src/lib/authHelpers.ts:signInWithCredentials` and `:completeOAuthSignIn` both call `await flushAuthState()` before returning
146: - `apps/frontend/src/lib/auth/signout.ts` is the canonical 7-step purge — copy that order, do not invent a new flow
147: - OAuth callback pages MUST use `window.location.href` on success, not `router.push` / `router.replace` (soft nav keeps the old tree mounted)
148: 
149: ### better-auth client/server boundary
150: 
151: `authClient` (from `lib/auth/authClient.ts`) transitively imports `better-auth/next-js` and `node:crypto` — both server-only. Never import `authClient` from any client-side auth utility (`signout.ts`, `authHelpers.ts`, etc.). Clear better-auth cookies via `document.cookie` directly. The ChunkLoadError in 1.2.2 came from violating this.
152: 
153: ### RTK Query auth-guard pattern
154: 
155: `shouldFetchUser = Boolean(accessToken && accessToken.length > 0)` — never use `isAuthenticated` alone for guarding queries. Stale persist rehydration can leave `isAuthenticated: true` with `accessToken: null`. The dev-only `console.warn` in `apiSlice.ts:prepareHeaders` surfaces this and must stay.
156: 
157: ### OAuth profile preservation
158: 
159: `createOrUpdateUserWithOAuth` and `createOrUpdateUser` must NEVER overwrite `name` or `image` on update — only fill them in if the existing value is empty. Custom uploads (S3) and renamed profiles belong to the user, not the OAuth provider. `emailVerified` is always refreshed.
