392: ## Additional Constraints from .cursor/rules/ (read-only source)
393: 
394: ### Backend Module Architecture
395: - Feature modules live under `apps/backend/src/app/modules/` with structure: controller, service, routes, validation schemas.
396: - Routes register ONLY in `apps/backend/src/app/routes` — never register ad-hoc routes elsewhere.
397: - Controllers must be thin; all business logic belongs in services.
398: - Services use Prisma client from shared singleton; handle transactions explicitly when needed.
399: - Zod for request body, param, and query validation; reject early on failure.
400: 
401: ### Database Operations
402: - **Prefer Prisma ORM** (`findMany`, `create`, `update`, `delete`, `upsert`, `count`, etc.) for new database operations — typed queries provide better type safety, refactoring support, and readability.
403: - **Keep existing `$queryRaw` / `$executeRaw` calls as-is** — do not rewrite working raw SQL unless there is a specific performance or correctness issue.
404: - **When raw SQL is needed** (pgvector similarity, complex aggregations, CTEs not supported by Prisma):
405:   - Use template literal syntax for SQL injection prevention: `WHERE email = ${email}`
406:   - Use `prisma.$queryRaw<Type[]>` for proper typing.
407:   - Select only required fields; never use `SELECT *`.
408:   - Use `LIMIT ${limit} OFFSET ${skip}` for pagination; never return unbounded lists.
409: - **EXCEPTION — OAuth operations MUST keep standard Prisma Client upsert:**
410:   - `createAccount()`, `createOrUpdateUser()`, `createOrUpdateUserWithOAuth()`
411:   - Changing these to raw queries causes P2002 unique constraint errors.
412: 
413: ### TypedSQL & Raw SQL Files
414: - Raw SQL statements live in `apps/backend/prisma/sql/` with ONE statement per file.
415: - File names must be valid JavaScript identifiers (no leading dashes) because they become generated function names.
416: - Use positional parameters `$1`, `$2` with optional `-- @param {Type} $1:name` comments.
417: - After adding/modifying SQL, run `yarn db:generate` to regenerate typed functions.
418: - Import generated functions from `@prisma/client/sql`.
419: - Execute typed queries with `prisma.$queryRawTyped(queryName(...params))` or `prisma.$queryRaw(...)`.
420: - Always apply pending migrations BEFORE running `prisma generate --sql`.
421: - Every new TypedSQL query must have at least one test verifying shape and performance assumptions.
422: - Above any raw query usage, add a comment referencing the originating `.sql` file.
423: 
424: ### Frontend Component & Design Standards
425: - Prefer Next.js Server Components; add `"use client"` ONLY when interactivity or state is required.
426: - Use `next/image` and `next/font`; stream large UI with Suspense to avoid unnecessary client bundles.
427: - Consult `docs/UI_DESIGN.md` BEFORE creating new pages or components.
428: - Component taxonomy:
429:   - `components/auth/` — Authentication related
430:   - `components/layout/` — Navigation, headers, sidebars
431:   - `components/ui/` — ShadCN primitives
432:   - `components/customUI/` — Custom components
433: - Design system: OKLCH color system, `max-w-[1440px]` container width, established Typography heading scales.
434: - Use existing hover effects (lift, scale, glow) and transitions.
435: - SEO: use Metadata API; ensure canonical URLs; plan sitemap + robots when routes stabilize.
436: - Accessibility: WCAG 2.1 AA compliance, proper ARIA labels, roles, focus states, keyboard navigation.
437: 
438: ### Sonner Toast & Error Handling Patterns
439: - Use Sonner via ToastProvider functions ONLY:
440:   - `showErrorToast`, `showSuccessToast` from `@/components/providers/ToastProvider`
441:   - `showApiErrorToast` from `@/lib/errorHandling`
442: - NEVER import `toast` directly from `sonner`.
443: - Use custom error handling hooks:
444:   - `useErrorHandler` for generic errors
445:   - `useQueryErrorHandler` for RTK Query queries
446:   - `useMutationErrorHandler` for mutations
447: - Smart retry: auto-retry on network/server errors, manual retry for client errors.
448: - Error classification: Network (retry), Client 4xx (fix required), Server 5xx (retry).
449: - All auth methods must use try/catch with `ApiError` for consistent error responses.
450: - Feature-specific error classes must extend `ApiError` with standardized format:
451:   ```typescript
452:   {
453:     success: false,
454:     message: string,
455:     statusCode: number,
456:     errorCode?: string,
457:     details?: object,
458:     timestamp: string
459:   }
460:   ```
461: 
462: ### Production-Ready Security & Performance Standards
463: - Debug logging is allowed ONLY in development; always gate with `process.env.NODE_ENV !== "production"`.
464: - Replace all `any` types with proper interfaces (e.g., `AuthenticatedRequest`).
465: - Apply feature-specific rate limiters to all mutation endpoints, especially uploads.
466: - Use `performanceMonitor` middleware and add `X-Response-Time` headers.
467: - Health check endpoints must exist:
468:   - `/api/health` — Basic health status
469:   - `/api/health/detailed` — Full system health
470:   - `/api/health/live` — Kubernetes liveness probe
471:   - `/api/health/ready` — Kubernetes readiness probe
472: - BigInt handling: cast to integer in SQL for JSON serialization to avoid issues.
473: - Memory monitoring: track heap usage and memory thresholds in health checks.
474: 
475: ### pgvector Detailed Rules
476: - Only run similarity queries if `USE_PGVECTOR=true`.
477: - `PaperChunk.embedding` column type is `vector`; migrations manage any transition from JSON fallback.
478: - Use a service helper to format float arrays into vector literals (`[x,y,z]`).
479: - Similarity operators: `<->` (L2), `<=>` (cosine), `<#>` (negative inner product). Align index operator class with chosen operator.
480: - Create IVF index (`ivfflat`) only after sufficient data volume; document chosen `lists` parameter.
481: - Limit result sets (e.g., `LIMIT 10`); avoid full vector scans.
482: - Guard against mismatched dimensionality; validate embedding array length before insert.
483: - Add round-trip test (insert + similarity query) when modifying embedding logic.
484: 
485: ### Auth Specifics
486: - Frontend authentication state is managed via Redux Toolkit (in addition to NextAuth session).
487: - OAuth account creation MUST use standard Prisma upsert pattern; do NOT convert to raw SQL.
488: - Password strength indicators on register forms.
489: - Auth guards for protected routes.
490: - All auth functions must have JSDoc comments.
491: - Authentication-related code requires minimum 90% test coverage.
492: - Comprehensive integration tests required for all auth endpoints and flows.
493: 
494: ### Role-Based Access Control (Phase 5+)
495: - Use the `requireRole(role)` factory from `apps/backend/src/app/middleware/requireRole.ts` for new RBAC routes. Convenience wrappers: `requireTeamLead`, `requireAdmin`.
496: - Apply the middleware AFTER `authMiddleware` in the route chain (RBAC needs an authenticated user first).
497: - Reject with `ApiError(403, "Insufficient permissions. Required: {role}, got: {userRole}")` — do not silently 200.
498: - For per-resource ownership checks (e.g. "only the workspace owner can edit settings"), perform the check inside the service via raw SQL or Prisma where/select, not in the middleware.
499: - For frontend role gating in `AppSidebar`, set `minRole: USER_ROLES.TEAM_LEAD` on the navigation item — `hasRoleAccess` handles the rest.
500: - Use `lib/auth/roles.ts` constants (`USER_ROLES.RESEARCHER`, etc.) and `hasRoleAccess(userRole, requiredRole)` — never compare role strings directly.
501: 
502: ### Email Delivery (Phase 5+)
503: - Transactional emails route through `emailService` in `apps/backend/src/app/shared/emailService.ts`.
504: - Dispatcher priority: Resend (if `RESEND_API_KEY` is set in env) → existing SMTP/Gmail transporter.
505: - Resend uses the built-in `fetch` API (`https://api.resend.com/emails`); no SDK dependency.
506: - Never add new SMTP providers without keeping Gmail as the fallback — never break local dev for users without the env var.
507: - New email templates are methods on `EmailService` (e.g. `sendTeamInvitationEmail(data)`); HTML is inlined in the method for now. If a template gets large, refactor to a `templates/` directory but keep the dispatcher call signature stable.
508: - Email send failures are logged but NEVER thrown — the main flow (invitation, etc.) must complete even if email delivery fails. Surface failures via `console.error` in dev, silent in production.
509: 
510: ### Workflow & Documentation Discipline
511: - Follow phase discipline strictly; see `Roadmap.md` before starting new features.
512: - Ship only in-phase work; defer out-of-scope requests unless they unblock the current milestone.
513: - Prefer shipping a thin vertical slice over broad incomplete scaffolding.
514: - Do NOT create README.md, OPTIMIZATION.md, CHANGELOG.md, or PERFORMANCE.md files for minor updates or every change.
515: - Inline documentation only; comments explain WHY not WHAT.
516: - Quality gates before merge:
517:   1. `yarn build` succeeds
518:   2. `yarn type-check` clean
519:   3. `yarn lint` zero errors
520:   4. Tests pass; add/adjust tests for new logic
521:   5. No secrets committed
522:   6. No obvious N+1 or unbounded queries
523:   7. WCAG 2.1 AA for new UI components
524:   8. Migrations are additive (backwards compatible)
525:   9. Update public docs (README, SCHEMA, ENVIRONMENT) for changed public behavior
526:   10. Keep PR scope tight with summary + checklist
