610: ## Query Performance Rules — Target: <50ms per Prisma query event
611: 
612: ### Verified Current State
613: - Prisma singleton is already globalThis-cached in `apps/backend/src/app/shared/prisma.ts`. Do not rewrite it as a plain module-level `new PrismaClient`.
614: - Adapter is `@prisma/adapter-pg` (node-postgres TCP pooling). DO NOT switch back to `@prisma/adapter-ppg` (HTTP-based, no keep-alive, 1500-2500ms per query from Bangladesh to US East).
615: - `PaperChunk.embedding` is enabled via `Unsupported("vector")`. HNSW index is created via migration.
616: - There are two `paper.service.ts` files. Active file is `apps/backend/src/app/modules/papers/paper.service.ts` (imported by `paper.controller.ts`).
617: - `@prisma/sqlcommenter-query-insights` is installed and wired into the singleton for Query Insights attribution.
618: - `prisma/seed.js` was modified to import `PrismaPg` adapter + generated client instead of raw `@prisma/client` (Prisma 7 requires adapter for client instantiation).
619: 
620: ### Terminal Query-Time Visibility
621: - The singleton registers a Prisma `$on('query')` listener in development.
622: - Any query event over 50ms is logged to the terminal as:
623:   `[SLOW QUERY] {duration}ms | {query first 150 chars} | params: {params first 80 chars}`
624: - This logging is the primary measurement tool — do not remove it.
625: - After each optimization, restart the backend and hit the affected endpoints; watch the terminal for slow-query warnings before/after.
626: 
627: ### Select Discipline
628: - All list queries must use explicit `select`.
629: - Never fetch `embedding` or binary file content in list views.
630: - PaperChunk list views select `id, content, page, idx, paperId` only.
631: 
632: ### Relation Loading
633: - Add `relationLoadStrategy: 'join'` only to `findMany` calls. It is invalid on `findFirst`, `create`, `update`, `upsert`.
634: - Keep explicit `select` inside every `include`.
635: 
636: ### Pagination
637: - Cursor-based pagination for papers, search, workspaces, notifications, and activity logs.
638: - Keep offset pagination only where `skip` is bounded by a small constant (e.g., cursor exclusion `skip: 1`).
639: 
640: ### Indexes
641: - New indexes use `CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY IF NOT EXISTS`.
642: - Verify exact table/column case against `schema.prisma`.
643: - HNSW vector index uses `vector_cosine_ops` with `m = 16, ef_construction = 64`.
644: 
645: ### Version Alignment
646: - Keep `@prisma/client`, `prisma`, and `@prisma/adapter-*` on the same minor version.
647: 
648: ### Verification Workflow
649: 1. Apply one optimization at a time.
650: 2. Restart `yarn dev:backend`.
651: 3. Hit the affected endpoint(s) from the frontend or with `curl`.
652: 4. Check the terminal for `[SLOW QUERY]` output.
653: 5. Confirm duration dropped below 50ms before moving to the next fix.
654: 6. Run `yarn type-check` and `yarn lint` after each significant change.
