658: ## Local Development Database
659: 
660: ### Database Setup
661: 
662: **Primary: Prisma Postgres (Cloud)** — used for both local dev and production
663: - `DATABASE_URL` = Accelerate endpoint in `.env` (runtime queries via proxy)
664: - `DIRECT_DATABASE_URL` = Direct PostgreSQL URL for migrations and adapter
665: - No local database needed — Prisma Cloud manages it
666: 
667: **Fallback: PostgreSQL 18 in WSL** (for offline dev or cloud issues)
668: - Install: `sudo apt install -y postgresql-18 postgresql-18-pgvector`
669: - Start:   `sudo pg_ctlcluster 18 main start`
670: - Stop:    `sudo pg_ctlcluster 18 main stop`
671: - Status:  `sudo pg_lsclusters`
672: - Default port: 5432
673: 
674: ### Database Initialization (after fresh install)
675: ```bash
676: # Create the database
677: sudo -u postgres psql -c "ALTER USER postgres PASSWORD 'admin';"
678: sudo -u postgres psql -c "CREATE DATABASE scholarflow_dev;"
679: 
680: # Enable required extensions
681: sudo -u postgres psql -d scholarflow_dev -c "CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector;"
682: sudo -u postgres psql -d scholarflow_dev -c "CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS pg_trgm;"
683: 
684: # Run migrations (overriding DATABASE_URL for local introspection)
685: DATABASE_URL="postgres://postgres:admin@localhost:5432/scholarflow_dev" yarn db:migrate
686: 
687: # Generate client and seed
688: yarn db:generate --sql
689: DATABASE_URL="postgres://postgres:admin@localhost:5432/scholarflow_dev" yarn db:seed
690: ```
691: 
692: ### Environment Strategy
693: - `.env` → Local development (`DIRECT_DATABASE_URL = postgres://postgres:admin@localhost:5432/scholarflow_dev`)
694: - `.env.production` → Cloud/Production (`DIRECT_DATABASE_URL` points to Prisma Cloud or deployed DB)
695: - The PG adapter picks up `DIRECT_DATABASE_URL` from whichever `.env` is loaded
696: - Never commit `.env` or `.env.production` (already in `.gitignore`)
697: 
698: ### Migration Discipline
699: - ALWAYS use `yarn db:migrate` — never `prisma db push`
700: - Fresh local DB = all migrations apply cleanly → no drift
701: - If drift appears locally: create reconciliation migration via `prisma migrate dev --create-only --name <name>`
702: - If drift appears on cloud: create a reconciliation migration, do NOT reset
703: - `prisma.config.ts` uses `DATABASE_URL` for migration, `DIRECT_DATABASE_URL` for directUrl
704: - Run `yarn db:generate --sql` after every migration
705: - When `prisma migrate dev` prompts for a new migration name (no pending migrations), press Ctrl+C and use `prisma migrate dev --create-only --name <name>` instead, then `prisma migrate deploy` to apply
706: 
707: ### Migration Drift (learned the hard way)
708: The schema in `schema.prisma` has accumulated columns and tables that were added to the production database via `prisma db push` (bypassing migration history). This causes `ColumnNotFound` errors when migrating a new database. Detection:
709: ```bash
710: # Compare current DB columns with schema
711: psql "postgres://postgres:admin@localhost:5432/scholarflow_dev" -At -c "SELECT column_name FROM information_schema.columns WHERE table_name = '<ModelName>' AND table_schema = 'public' ORDER BY ordinal_position;"
712: ```
713: Fix: Run `prisma migrate dev --create-only --name reconcile_schema_drift` with `DATABASE_URL` pointing to the drift-free database. Review the generated SQL carefully — it may contain destructive operations (column drops, type changes) if the schema diverged. Apply with `prisma migrate deploy`.
714: 
715: ### Adapter Configuration
716: - Adapter: `@prisma/adapter-pg` with `pg` driver (TCP connection pooling)
717: - Connection: passes `DIRECT_DATABASE_URL` to adapter
718: - Works with any standard `postgres://` URL (local, cloud, any provider)
719: - Pooling: `pg` driver pools TCP connections natively (no extra config needed)
720: - DO NOT use `@prisma/adapter-ppg` — no HTTP keep-alive, 1500ms+ per query with cloud DB latency from Bangladesh
721: 
722: ### Seed Script
723: - Location: `apps/backend/prisma/seed.js` (CommonJS)
724: - Script: `yarn db:seed` → runs `ts-node prisma/seed.js`
725: - Uses `@prisma/adapter-pg` with `PrismaPg` adapter (imported from generated client)
726: - Default password for all demo users: `password123`
727: - Demo users: admin@scholarflow.com, researcher@scholarflow.com, pro.researcher@scholarflow.com, teamlead@scholarflow.com
728: - Must override `DATABASE_URL` + `DIRECT_DATABASE_URL` to local URL when seeding local DB (WSL fallback) or Prisma Cloud URLs when seeding cloud DB
729: 
730: ### Performance Verification Workflow
731: 1. Ensure local PG18 is running: `sudo pg_ctlcluster 18 main start`
732: 2. Start backend: `yarn dev:backend`
733: 3. Hit any DB endpoint from dashboard or curl
734: 4. Terminal shows `[SLOW QUERY] {duration}ms` for any query >50ms
735: 5. On localhost: expect <10ms (vs 240ms to US East)
736: 6. On deployed US East backend: expect <50ms
737: 7. If >50ms with local DB, check for missing indexes or N+1 queries
